         o   (A) Gin poles shall have a documented inspection annually by a qualiﬁed
             person;
         o   (B) In addition to the annual inspection, the employer shall designate a
           competent person who shall visually inspect the gin pole and rigging prior to
           each use, and during use, to make sure it is in safe operating condition. Any
             deﬁciencies shall be repaired before use continues;
         o  (C) During each inspection, the qualiﬁed or competent
            person shall inspect the legs and bracing members for bends or distortion;
         o  (D) During each inspection, the qualiﬁed or competent person shall
             inspect the straightness tolerances for the overall assembly (including leg
           and bracing members);
         o   (E) During each inspection, the qualiﬁed or competent person shall visually
